Accepts a name waiting in the queue as a topic of its own, with its intake: what it is about, who it is for, how it is grouped, how many cards it gets and what it should cover. Code makes the slug from the name, normalizes the category, writes them to the topic, and stores your intake as a record that the topic's tadpole and the curriculum chat work from. The topic then waits for its turn in the queue; nothing is written for it yet. Accept only once find_topics_by_name, and find_topics_by_meaning when the name leaves it open, show no topic that already covers the subject for this angle, and reuse a category list_categories shows rather than coin a near-duplicate. Name in builds_on the topics that share its subject, so its tadpole starts from what they already gathered.
